                                "sense_id": "e50c0a69-18e0-3890-b3db-28eecf49f6ba",
                                "text": "Thou wondrous harper, that hast thrilled my heart, […]\nAnd made me all athrob with ecstasy,—"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "46664f48-8305-42f4-95d7-cb6fb5279253",
                                "sense_id": "e50c0a69-18e0-3890-b3db-28eecf49f6ba",
                                "text": "The great test was on, whether such a nation could live, and Boston was athrob with love of country and eagerness to sacrifice."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d0419d9e-2bd4-480b-adac-e313451da853",
                                "sense_id": "e50c0a69-18e0-3890-b3db-28eecf49f6ba",
                                "text": "[…] all the earth was blurred in darkness and the sky a-throb with starlight, for it was yet an hour until the rising of the moon."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "975a51ec-914b-44b6-a7a8-6b87314244c0",
                                "sense_id": "e50c0a69-18e0-3890-b3db-28eecf49f6ba",
                                "text": "I have my sore wound, all my length of arm\na-throb with lancing pain;"
                            }
                        ]
